eir period, despite the fact that even light use is known to cause gut and gastrointestinal issues.*<br><br><br>The problem? Painkillers can't fix your hormones, and they definitely don’t fill nutrient gaps. That’s why the pain keeps coming back just as strong every month — along with the bloating, fatigue, and mood swings that make periods even harder.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><br><strong><u>But here's the good news:<br></u></strong><br><br>Leading specialists in menstrual health have found that by tackling all three underlying triggers at once, you can get ahead of cramps before they start — becoming the woman who barely notices them and doesn’t have to battle PMS or other monthly symptoms— thanks to a breakthrough approach.</p></span></div><div data-rid="73ee2dc7-577f-4d06-b7d7-9cffcbdb62b3" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" tabindex="0" role="link" class="r-ozft7y alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-color:#2A2A2A;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-fontsize:12px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-textdecoration:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-fontfamily:Quicksand;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-fontweight:700;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-lineheight:16px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-textshadow:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d7-b73f-26639a2f7dc0-attributes-textstroke:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f775258-2b0d-43d